From: Amoeba STB Mini Monitor
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: meson-gxl: enable I2C_A on B860H D1/E1 pins

The GXL pinctrl maps I2C_A SDA to GPIODV_24 and SCK to GPIODV_25.
These pins are also UART_B TX/RX, so keep UART_B disabled while I2C_A
owns the pins. Enable the I2C controller and select the I2C_A pin group.

Based on the B860H DTS in ophub/linux-6.12.y (blob
956941fb21fe12e0527ebc37aa19476a9f9b2ca8).

IMPORTANT: this configures SoC pins GPIODV_24/25. It does not prove that
the B860H board's X2 TTL header is physically routed to these exact pads.
Verify the PCB route before wiring or booting with the OLED attached.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905x-b860h.dts | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905x-b860h.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905x-b860h.dts
index 956941fb21fe..000000000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905x-b860h.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905x-b860h.dts
@@ -17,3 +17,19 @@
 &sdio_pwrseq {
     reset-gpios = <&gpio GPIODV_27 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Amoeba STB Mini Monitor:
+ * I2C_A SDA = GPIODV_24, SCK/SCL = GPIODV_25.
+ * These pads are shared with UART_B TX/RX.
+ */
+&uart_B {
+    status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&i2c_A {
+    pinctrl-0 = <&i2c_a_pins>;
+    pinctrl-names = "default";
+    clock-frequency = <100000>;
+    status = "okay";
+};
